body:
This is the script I used to reproduce it:
```
for i in $(seq 1 4000); do
    curl -HContent-Type:application/json -XPOST localhost:9200/test/test -d'{"test": "test"}'; echo
done

curl -XPOST localhost:9200/_refresh

curl -HContent-Type:application/json -XPOST 'localhost:9200/test/_update_by_query?refresh&pretty' -d'{
    "query":  {
        "match": {
            "test": "test"
        }
    },
    "script": {
        "inline": "ctx._source.foo=\"bar\""
    }
}'
```

That last one *should* return `4000` documents updated but it returns `1000`.

Better reproduction:
```
for i in $(seq 1 4000); do
    curl -HContent-Type:application/json -XPOST localhost:9200/test/test -d'{"test": "test"}'; echo
done

curl -XPOST localhost:9200/_refresh

curl -HContent-Type:application/json -XPOST 'localhost:9200/test/_update_by_query?refresh&pretty'


#This one it ok!
curl -HContent-Type:application/json -XPOST 'localhost:9200/_reindex?refresh&pretty' -d'{
    "source": {
        "index": "test"
    },
    "dest": {
        "index": "dest"
    }
}'


curl -HContent-Type:application/json -XPOST 'localhost:9200/dest/_delete_by_query?refresh&pretty' -d'{
    "query": {
        "match_all": {}
    }
}'
```

Shows that this effects `_update_by_query` and `_delete_by_query` but not `_reindex`.
